After my ascension I decided I wanted to try a new role... I had two
possibilites, rogue and monk.  I remembered that monk is a really hard
role in vanilla so on a whim I downloaded SLASH 'EM, as the wiki
suggested monks were easier there.
For all those who've never tried it... it's like vanilla on steroids,
or something.  Monks are really good with massive natural armor and
rapid intrinsic gain.  My first monk got to like XL 9 and the Oracle
level, easy, and would have gotten farther if not for human error.  I
do see how it's called unbalanced, though.  My first Monk was
generated with an oil lamp, so of course I knew what the magic lamps
were off the bat.  And I must say, it's a good thing they cost base
1000 zm, because Minetown had 1 and the Mall had _3_.  Goodness.
Lighting shops are a little too good, IMO.  But anyway, who else has
messed around with SLASH 'EM?  I'm still doing rogues in vanilla
(hooray for gatling daggers), but the new Monks are too cool to pass
up, and Undead Slayer looks great as well.  Am I destined to be
disappointed?


